+**Robust security measures:** Enhanced background checks through international intelligence sharing, biometric screening, and thorough interviews. Countries like Canada and Australia do this successfully without massive backlogs.
+
+**Fraud prevention:** Trained adjudicators catch inconsistencies better than overwhelmed ones. Legal representation actually reduces false claims because people know genuine cases have better outcomes than fraudulent ones.
+
+**Transparency and accountability:** Independent oversight of the process builds public confidence. We can publish metrics on approval rates, processing times, and security incidents.
+
+The key insight is this: security and fairness aren't trade-offs; they reinforce each other. A transparent, well-funded system with proper due process is more secure because it's legitimate and effective. A chaotic system creates resentment and actually makes enforcement harder.
+
+We should never accept false choices between protecting people and protecting security.<|im_end|>
