+
+The problem is that allowing broad religious exemptions creates a race to the bottom. Every employer could claim religious exemptions—from healthcare to retirement benefits to workplace safety—based on their owner's beliefs. This disproportionately harms marginalized groups and workers with fewer job options. A same-sex couple might struggle to find employment in their area if most employers cite religious beliefs to deny them equal benefits.
+
