+
+The most effective measures combine legal prohibition with positive support systems. This means not just banning the harmful practice, but also ensuring access to affirming mental healthcare, family support programs, and community resources. We should be funding LGBTQ+ youth centers, training therapists in affirming practices, and creating school environments where young people feel safe.
+
+From a progressive standpoint, this is essential healthcare policy—protecting vulnerable people from harm while ensuring they have access to quality, affirming mental health services. We need federal legislation to establish consistent protections across all states, because right now gaps exist where vulnerable minors still lack legal safeguards. Additionally, we should support survivors through comprehensive mental health coverage—another reason universal healthcare is crucial. Everyone deserves access to trauma-informed care that validates their identity, regardless of their ability to pay. This is about collective welfare and social justice.<|im_end|>
